WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.540
Parallel Structure and Logical Comparisons

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:07.528
Lists match. Comparisons compare like with like.

00:00:08.728 --> 00:00:09.818
How to spot it

00:00:10.218 --> 00:00:12.506
A list or pair with one item missing

00:00:13.056 --> 00:00:14.956
Or a comparison with “than”

00:00:15.506 --> 00:00:19.493
It’s testing: matching forms and logical comparisons

00:00:20.693 --> 00:00:21.459
The method

00:00:21.859 --> 00:00:24.291
Step 1: Find the other items

00:00:24.571 --> 00:00:25.698
What form are they?

00:00:26.248 --> 00:00:28.294
Step 2: Copy the form

00:00:28.574 --> 00:00:31.721
-ing, “to” + verb, noun or past tense.

00:00:32.271 --> 00:00:35.743
Step 3: Name both sides of a comparison

00:00:36.023 --> 00:00:38.972
Diet vs diet, not diet vs people.

00:00:39.522 --> 00:00:42.231
Step 4: Fix with that of / those of

00:00:42.511 --> 00:00:44.730
One thing: that. Many: those.

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:46.375
In a few words

00:00:46.525 --> 00:00:48.869
Match the form. Match the thing.

00:00:50.069 --> 00:00:50.851
The rules

00:00:51.251 --> 00:00:52.661
Lists use one form

00:00:52.941 --> 00:00:55.175
Wrong: to ask, examining, and draw

00:00:55.455 --> 00:00:58.153
Right: to ask, to examine, and to draw

00:00:58.703 --> 00:00:59.622
Pairs match

00:00:59.902 --> 00:01:03.345
Right: not only to cut costs but also to improve care

00:01:03.895 --> 00:01:05.261
Compare like with like

00:01:05.541 --> 00:01:09.386
Wrong: Tokyo’s population is larger than New York.

00:01:09.666 --> 00:01:12.540
Right: larger than that of New York

00:01:13.090 --> 00:01:15.575
that of = one, those of = many

00:01:15.855 --> 00:01:19.618
Right: her songs are longer than those of other singers

00:01:20.818 --> 00:01:21.879
Let’s try one

00:01:22.279 --> 00:01:28.247
Studies of ancient DNA show that the diet of early farmers in the region was less varied than ______

00:01:28.897 --> 00:01:32.512
What’s being compared? The diet of early farmers.

00:01:33.062 --> 00:01:38.802
Diet versus people: A. Those is plural: C. And D isn’t grammatical.

00:01:39.352 --> 00:01:44.581
That of the hunter-gatherers: a diet compared to a diet. Choice B.

00:01:45.781 --> 00:01:46.850
Common traps

00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:48.660
Thing vs person

00:01:48.940 --> 00:01:52.825
“Her paintings are brighter than Monet.” Compare paintings.

00:01:53.375 --> 00:01:54.471
The mixed list

00:01:54.751 --> 00:01:56.560
One item in a different form.

00:01:57.760 --> 00:02:00.700
Parallel Structure and Logical Comparisons

00:02:00.980 --> 00:02:03.324
Match the form. Match the thing.

00:02:03.874 --> 00:02:04.454
Spot it

00:02:04.654 --> 00:02:08.410
List or pair missing an item, or a “than” comparison

00:02:08.960 --> 00:02:09.667
Steps

00:02:09.867 --> 00:02:12.214
1. Find the form of the other items

00:02:12.494 --> 00:02:14.495
2. Copy that form exactly

00:02:14.775 --> 00:02:17.245
3. Name both sides of a comparison

00:02:17.525 --> 00:02:19.606
4. Fix with that of / those of

00:02:20.156 --> 00:02:20.881
Remember

00:02:21.081 --> 00:02:24.362
Lists: one form (to ask, to examine, to draw)

00:02:24.642 --> 00:02:26.861
not only … but also … must match

00:02:27.141 --> 00:02:28.507
Compare like with like

00:02:28.787 --> 00:02:31.880
that of = one; those of = many

00:02:32.430 --> 00:02:32.870
Trap

00:02:33.070 --> 00:02:34.977
Comparing a thing to a person

00:02:35.727 --> 00:02:39.145
